      "id": "gxrl7wy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals are electropositive elements that readily lose electrons to form positive cations.",
        "Non-metals are electronegative elements that gain or share electrons to form negative anions or covalent bonds.",
        "Metals form basic or amphoteric oxides, whereas non-metals form acidic or neutral oxides.",
        "The Reactivity Series ranks metals in decreasing order of their chemical reactivity.",
        "Highly reactive metals are extracted via electrolysis, while moderately reactive metals are reduced using carbon."
      ],
      "id": "umrcy7r"
    },
