      "content": "8. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mercury is the only liquid metal, while Bromine is the only liquid non-metal at room temperature.",
        "Sodium and Potassium are soft metals that can be cut with a knife and are stored under kerosene oil.",
        "Aqua Regia is a freshly prepared 3:1 mixture of concentrated HCl and concentrated HNO3 used to dissolve Gold and Platinum.",
        "Amphoteric oxides like Aluminium oxide (Al2O3) and Zinc oxide (ZnO) react with both acids and bases to produce salt and water."
      ],
      "id": "ez20jj2"
